-4-11-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":11,"verse":31,"english":"Hearing those words of that intelligent lord of monkeys, Dundhubhi, with reddened eyes spoke.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-11-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4011031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"db91ab8a82e6739c95fc5e0f615ea28a36df6c9b1d66a1e00e25e66fbca74556","compact":"9fa76cda756c7e4e8390216be2afcfeeb710f8b9647e7e1ad3480698cd2cdc89","nasal":"469f62409000f58696724f813f2e0661ebb79601cfcb9992fd601c6bacc214d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-11-32","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":11,"verse":32,"english":"O hero, it becomes you not to speak thus before your wives. Do you enter into conflict with me and your prowess shall be ascertained thereafter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-11-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4011032","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e79eb4a8a801b95d15025204f5a110a12b7945122c53725b0ea5cb5d157ccc6f","compact":"dc96bc13b2e179407c262a74beb1600346c8ddcd270bb36c8565875745384bb1","nasal":"dc96bc13b2e179407c262a74beb1600346c8ddcd270bb36c8565875745384bb1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-11-33","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":11,"verse":33,"english":"Or I shall suppress my wrath for this night and do you, O monkey, enjoy till the rise of the Sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-11-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4011033","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"825748e93e71190bf63c6f513e2199a062d552b78bffa86aafd3fc3b2f7f3221","compact":"1baf2579bce263323b0c21a57e3d202cefe14cb87238d83bb569e23b19f57034","nasal":"1baf2579bce263323b0c2