ful Raghava, of mighty arms-Laksmana's elder brother, lifting up easily with his thumb the dried frame of that Asura-Dundhubhi-hurled it at a distance of ten Yojanas.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.636,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-11-75","DUTT-4-11-77"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4011050","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84a6cdb1bdb2663b8640000b2bcc9d576bcc306bec112b195378460ebd2b1ded","compact":"ca89de5dd5168778bb69c7a3e5f80a553ca6526e4e88068e38fbd33a95604bb1","nasal":"f080171c71908927c52f827af9f462d9dd30e1e608694a3d74ee71df907e0ada"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-11-51","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":11,"verse":51,"english":"Beholding that Asura's body thrown thus, Sugrīva, again addressed to the heroic Rāma, before Lakşmaņa and the monkey herd, the following pregnant words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.897,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-11-78"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4011051","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0aaa6bb33faa5f331d46b32332fd9edf48da35490d800cdc0556d2b1b66326f5","compact":"4b3a9b0493fa04caf38db08ded7327dbf728e5c476539b70a8c0eaeda72d894f","nasal":"4b3a9b0493fa04caf38db08ded7327dbf728e5c476539b70a8c0eaeda72d894f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-11-52","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":11,"verse":52,"english":"Friend, formerly this body was wet and corpulent, and it was thrown with great difficulty by my brother Vāli, mad with voluptuousness. And unable am I to ascertain who is the mightier? There is a good deal of difference, O Rāghava, between a body, wet and dried.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.272,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-11-79","DUTT-4-11-81"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4011052","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"}